research/audit/wave12-dispatch/audit-refuter-cex-mean-value-equality-fails-for-a-vector-valued-function.prompt.md-2280-- **Why the intrinsic derivative is stated first.** The componentwise formula is
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/audit-refuter-cex-mean-value-equality-fails-for-a-vector-valued-function.prompt.md-2281-  the one used in computations, but it is tied to the standard basis, whereas the
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/audit-refuter-cex-mean-value-equality-fails-for-a-vector-valued-function.prompt.md-2282-  limit of the difference quotient is not. The intrinsic form is the one that
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/audit-refuter-cex-mean-value-equality-fails-for-a-vector-valued-function.prompt.md-2283-  survives when the domain is enlarged from an interval to a subset of
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/audit-refuter-cex-mean-value-equality-fails-for-a-vector-valued-function.prompt.md-2284-  $\mathbb{R}^{n}$, which is a later page of this track.
